# Holding the Door Open

Jason Lin's internship portfolio for Hope's Door NY. A single self-contained
web page: the twelve-month LinkedIn audit, the rebuilt engagement strategy,
and the system left behind for the team.

There is **no build step**. It is one HTML file plus two images, so any static
host will serve it as is.

---

## Run it on your computer

You need [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) installed (version 18 or newer).

```bash
npm run dev
```

Then open <http://localhost:3000>.

That is it. There are no dependencies to install first, because `npm run dev`
downloads a tiny static file server on demand.

If you would rather not use Node, any of these work just as well:

```bash
python3 -m http.server 3000     # Python
php -S localhost:3000           # PHP
npx --yes serve . -l 3000       # Node, without the script
```

> **Why a server at all?** Double-clicking `index.html` mostly works, but
> browsers apply stricter rules to `file://` pages, so serving it locally is a
> truer preview of the live site.

